VapourSynth-Retinex at 6bfbdd429159c85075dc4b08e0ac4e706470916b (r4 + "Fix
unexpected appending when sigma is specified", 2021-10-18, the last commit).
VapourBox task #113, docs/reports/task-113-retinex-sigma.

r4 (the only release with a Windows binary) starts MSR's sigma vector from the
defaults {25, 80, 250} and pushes each value the caller passes onto it, so
MSRCP(sigma=[X]) runs a four-scale retinex [25, 80, 250, X]. 6bfbdd42 starts
from an empty vector, so it runs [X]. The template always passes sigma (Shadow
Detail's slider), so the r4 DLL Windows used to ship filtered differently from
the macOS/Linux builds: about 10 8-bit levels apart at the default sigma 100.
Every platform now builds 6bfbdd42 from source.

This patch changes no code. It appends "(VapourBox: 6bfbdd42, sigma not
appended, task #113)" to the plugin's description (core.retinex.name), which is
how the deps scripts (a byte search of the binary) replace an r4 build or an
older unmarked one, and how the test tells this build from r4: API 3 plugins
report no version.

Applied by download-deps-{macos,linux}.sh and download-deps-windows.ps1 right
after the clone; each build fails if it stops applying or the marker is
missing afterwards.

diff --git a/source/VSPlugin.cpp b/source/VSPlugin.cpp
index fa76472..e64a15a 100644
--- a/source/VSPlugin.cpp
+++ b/source/VSPlugin.cpp
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 VS_EXTERNAL_API(void) VapourSynthPluginInit(VSConfigPlugin configFunc, VSRegisterFunction registerFunc, VSPlugin *plugin)
 {
     configFunc("com.vapoursynth.retinex", "retinex",
-        "Implementation of Retinex algorithm for VapourSynth.",
+        "Implementation of Retinex algorithm for VapourSynth. (VapourBox: 6bfbdd42, sigma not appended, task #113)",
         VAPOURSYNTH_API_VERSION, 1, plugin);
 
     registerFunc("MSRCP", "input:clip;sigma:float[]:opt;lower_thr:float:opt;upper_thr:float:opt;fulls:int:opt;fulld:int:opt;chroma_protect:float:opt", MSRCPCreate, nullptr, plugin);
